&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optical &amp;amp; Semiconductor Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;£43,000–£50,000 depending on experience + EMI Share Options + Private Healthcare + Pension&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help build the technology enabling the next generation of semiconductors.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Infinitesima, we&#39;re developing advanced metrology systems that allow the world&#39;s leading semiconductor companies to measure and understand materials at the nanoscale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Production Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to build, integrate and test the precision optical, electro-mechanical and photonic assemblies that form the heart of our breakthrough technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a high-volume production role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work on complex, high-value systems, collaborating closely with engineers and scientists to solve manufacturing challenges, improve processes and ensure our products perform to the highest standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy combining hands-on build expertise with problem-solving and continuous improvement, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reward &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous EMI share option scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Death in service benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Abingdon, Oxfordshire, Infinitesima is a rapidly growing deep-tech company developing next-generation metrology solutions for the semiconductor industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading global investors, including Applied Ventures, we&#39;re combining world-class engineering, physics and software expertise to solve some of the industry&#39;s most complex measurement challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manufacture and test complex optical, cabling, and electro-mechanical sub-assemblies, ensuring compliance with manufacturing, assembly, and test procedures, quality requirements, and performance standards, while contributing to continuous process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, investigate, and resolve manufacturing issues by leading root cause analysis and permanent corrective actions, collaborating with engineering and cross-functional support teams to deliver effective, long-term solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive manufacturing process improvements by designing safe trials, validating process changes, and updating standards and controls to improve quality, reliability, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex system integration activities, validating module and system performance, resolving integration issues, and ensuring manufacturing readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support colleagues, ensure BoM kit readiness, and maintain high standards of housekeeping and health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to support product development, new product introduction (NPI), and the successful transfer of new products and processes into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of production commitments by ensuring high-quality, right-first-time assembly and test, coordinating priorities, and removing barriers to schedule achievement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll come from within semiconductor equipment, photonics, scientific instrumentation, aerospace, medical devices or another advanced technology manufacturing environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production Engineer experience, or a minimum of five years&#39; experience in a Senior Manufacturing Technician role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with optical systems, fibre optics, lasers, electronics, and electro-mechanical integration and test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, integrating, and testing complex, high-value technology products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in cleanroom manufacturing and controlled environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical approach to troubleshooting and root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience transitioning products from development into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of manufacturing quality systems and process controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret engineering drawings, specifications, and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and testing precision assemblies to high quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability in manufacturing engineering and process development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and application of Lean, Six Sigma, or equivalent improvement methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Semiconductor equipment manufacturing background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of AFM, metrology, photonics, or scientific instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPC wiring and soldering certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background supporting low-volume, high-complexity products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
