&lt;li&gt;Develop and enhance our FP&amp;amp;A reporting stack, including tools such as Looker, AI-based apps and underlying data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business questions into robust dashboards and self-service analytics to service business stakeholders such as the retail management organization and the logistics team in collaboration with the respective finance business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve our planning process by maintaining and further developing data models and process flows in our enterprise planning solution “Pigment”.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge and reconcile data across systems such as Microsoft Dynamics, Pigment and Looker to increase alignment between business stakeholders by working towards a harmonized KPI framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce reliance on Excel by building structured, reliable reporting layers in the aforementioned toolset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a key interface between Finance, Data, and Engineering teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 years of experience in FP&amp;amp;A, Controlling, or Data Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Masters in Finance, Economics, and/or STEM is a nice to have&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in data, systems, and process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with BI tools (ideally Looker) is a must and enterprise planning software &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;(e.g. Pigment, Anaplan, Workday Adaptive Planning)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work with data models and process automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with attention to detail and data quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex data into clear, business-relevant insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
