&lt;h6&gt;SUITSUPPLY is a global leader in men&#39;s fashion, specializing in high-quality suits and menswear, available online and in stores worldwide. Our mission is to empower people to look and feel their best, leveraging cutting-edge technology to provide exceptional customer experiences. At SUITSUPPLY, innovation drives us, and craftsmanship, quality, and service define us. Are you a natural leader with a passion for technology and team success? Join us!&amp;nbsp;We are looking for an experienced Software Engineering Manager to lead our dynamic engineering teams and help drive our digital transformation as we scale up to become the global style destination. If you’re passionate about technology, agile methodologies, and empowering teams to achieve their best, this is the perfect opportunity for you!&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;What you will do&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and Inspire: Coach, develop, and guide multiple IT development teams, fostering a culture of autonomy, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Quality Delivery: Oversee the delivery of high-quality software products that meet business goals and customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Boost Team Performance: Increase team velocity by setting up personal development plans, facilitating knowledge sharing, and promoting technical growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate for Success: Work closely with other Engineering Managers, Software Architects, Product Owners and Director of Engineering to define and execute a long-term Tech &amp;amp; Product vision and strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simplify and Scale: Simplify our complex technical legacy systems and support our growth from a startup mentality to a mature, scalable organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Who you are&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of experience managing and steering Agile teams of 5+ engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science or significant hands-on development experience with a solid track record of career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in Agile methodologies, with knowledge of coding in multiple languages (hands-on coding is not required for this role!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in line management, nurturing high-performing teams, and enabling both personal and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an international environment, with the ability to communicate effectively on both technical and non-technical topics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing 3-5 high-performing, autonomous teams to drive increased velocity and deliver results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attracting and hiring top talent to build strong, dynamic engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering high-quality software solutions with a focus on continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling our tech infrastructure by leveraging SaaS, cloud-native technologies, and simplifying legacy systems to support growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
